# ==============================================================================
# BAOBAB Enterprise Platform
# Git Attributes — enforce LF line endings repo-wide
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every shell script in this repository was found committed with CRLF line
# endings (scripts/verify.sh, scripts/summary.sh, scripts/post-create.sh,
# scripts/bootstrap.sh, scripts/verify-image.sh, config/resolve.sh, and all
# of config/bashrc.d/*.sh). This is not cosmetic — it is a real, build-
# breaking defect:
#
#   1. Any of these scripts executed directly via their own shebang line
#      (e.g. the Dockerfile's `RUN baobab-verify` build-time gate, which
#      execs /usr/local/bin/baobab-verify directly) fails immediately: the
#      kernel reads the shebang as "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r", tries to exec
#      an interpreter literally named "bash\r", and fails with
#      `env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory`.
#   2. Even when a script is instead invoked via an explicit `bash
#      script.sh` (bypassing the shebang), bash's own parser can still
#      choke on the embedded \r: a trailing \r glues onto whatever token
#      precedes it (e.g. `for arg in "$@"; do\r` is parsed as the single
#      malformed token `do\r`, not `do` followed by a newline), producing
#      a hard syntax error rather than a warning.
#
# Without this file, a contributor's editor or OS defaulting to CRLF on
# save (or a Windows git checkout without core.autocrlf configured) will
# silently reintroduce the exact same class of bug on the next commit that
# touches any of these files — Git otherwise preserves whatever line
# endings are staged, it does not normalize them on its own.
#
# `eol=lf` below normalizes line endings to LF both on checkout and on
# commit, regardless of the committing contributor's local git config.
# ==============================================================================

# Default: treat everything Git considers text as text, normalize to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, for clarity — these are exactly the file types this project
# generates or hand-edits as text.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.lock    text eol=lf
.python-version text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never let line-ending normalization touch these,
# even if `* text=auto` above would otherwise guess wrong for a given file.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.ico     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.svg     text eol=lf